# PRIVACY POLICY - KHANEME BUSINESS APP (MESS OWNERS)

**Last Updated: February 15, 2026**

## 1. INTRODUCTION

Welcome to the Khaneme Business App ("we," "our," or "us"). This Privacy Policy is specifically for mess owners and operators who use our business-facing platform to list and manage their mess establishments on Khaneme.

This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, disclose, and safeguard your information when you use our business mobile application (the "Business App").

This Privacy Policy complies with the Information Technology Act, 2000, the Information Technology (Reasonable Security Practices and Procedures and Sensitive Personal Data or Information) Rules, 2011, and the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 (DPDP Act).

By using our Business App, you consent to the data practices described in this policy.

## 2. ABOUT KHANEME BUSINESS APP

The Khaneme Business App is a platform for mess owners to:
- Create and manage their mess profiles
- List thalis (meal plans) and dishes
- Update operating hours and contact information
- View analytics about profile views and engagement
- Manage their presence on the Khaneme consumer discovery platform

## 3. INFORMATION WE COLLECT

### 3.1 Business Registration Information
During onboarding, we collect the following information:

**Mess Establishment Details:**
- **Mess Name**: Official name of your mess establishment
- **Owner Name**: Full name of the mess owner/operator
- **Owner Phone Number**: Contact number for verification and communication
- **Owner Email Address**: For account management and important notifications
- **FSSAI Number**: Food Safety and Standards Authority of India license number (optional but recommended)
- **Location (GPS Coordinates)**: Precise location of your mess for mapping and discovery
- **Physical Address**: Complete address including street, area, city, state, PIN code
- **Working Hours**: Daily operating hours and meal timings
- **Mess Photos**: Up to 5 photographs of your mess establishment

**Purpose of Collection:**
- Verification of your mess establishment
- Creation of your public profile on the consumer app
- Enabling location-based discovery for consumers
- Communication regarding your account and services
- Compliance with legal and regulatory requirements

### 3.2 Thali and Menu Information
After onboarding, you provide:
- **Thali Details**: Meal plan names, descriptions, and pricing
- **Dish Information**: Individual dishes, ingredients, preparation methods
- **Menu Updates**: Additions, deletions, and modifications to your offerings
- **Availability Information**: Current meal availability and timing

This information is displayed to consumers on the Khaneme consumer app.

### 3.3 Device and Technical Information
We automatically collect:
- Device information (model, operating system, unique identifiers)
- App usage data (features used, time spent, login frequency)
- IP address and approximate location
- Log data (access times, errors, crashes)
- Performance metrics

### 3.4 Analytics and Engagement Data
We track and provide you with analytics about:
- **Profile Views**: Number of times consumers viewed your mess profile
- **Thali Clicks**: Number of times consumers clicked on your thali offerings
- **Aggregate Demographics**: Age ranges and gender distribution of viewers (e.g., "60% viewers are 18-25 years old")
- **Engagement Metrics**: Time spent viewing your profile, photo views

**Important**: We do NOT provide you with individual consumer identities or personal information. All analytics are aggregated and anonymized.

### 3.5 Communication Data
- Support tickets and inquiries you submit
- Feedback and suggestions
- Correspondence with our team

### 3.6 Payment Information (If Applicable in Future)
Currently, the Business App is free. If we introduce paid features in the future:
- Payment method details
- Billing address
- Transaction history
- GST information (if applicable)

## 4. HOW WE USE YOUR INFORMATION

We use the collected information for the following purposes:

### 4.1 Service Provision
- **Profile Creation**: Create and maintain your public mess profile on the consumer app
- **Discovery**: Enable consumers to find your mess through location-based search
- **Information Display**: Show your thalis, dishes, timings, and photos to consumers
- **Verification**: Verify the legitimacy of your mess establishment
- **Account Management**: Manage your Business App account and access

### 4.2 Analytics and Insights
- **Performance Tracking**: Track how many consumers view your profile
- **Engagement Metrics**: Measure interest in your thalis and offerings
- **Dashboard Analytics**: Provide you with insights about consumer engagement
- **Aggregate Demographics**: Share anonymized demographic trends of your viewers

### 4.3 Communication
- **Account Notifications**: Important updates about your account or profile
- **Platform Updates**: Information about new features or changes to the Business App
- **Support Responses**: Replies to your inquiries and support requests
- **Verification Communications**: Contact you to verify your mess establishment

### 4.4 Platform Improvement
- **User Experience**: Improve the Business App interface and functionality
- **Feature Development**: Understand which features are most useful to mess owners
- **Quality Assurance**: Identify and fix bugs or technical issues

### 4.5 Legal and Compliance
- **Regulatory Compliance**: Comply with applicable food safety, business, and data protection laws
- **Fraud Prevention**: Detect and prevent fraudulent listings or activities
- **Dispute Resolution**: Handle complaints or disputes related to your mess
- **Legal Obligations**: Respond to legal requests or court orders

## 5. DATA SHARING AND DISCLOSURE

### 5.1 Public Information on Consumer App
The following information is displayed publicly to consumers on the Khaneme consumer app:

**Publicly Visible Information:**
- Mess name
- Location (on map) and address
- Working hours and meal timings
- Mess photos (up to 5)
- Thali names, descriptions, and prices
- Dish details and ingredients
- FSSAI number (if provided)

**NOT Publicly Visible:**
- Owner's personal name (only mess name is shown)
- Owner's email address
- Owner's phone number
- Any personal identification documents

### 5.2 Analytics Data You Receive
We provide you with aggregated, anonymized analytics:
- Total number of profile views
- Aggregate demographic information (age ranges, gender percentages)
- Engagement metrics (thali clicks, photo views)

**We do NOT provide:**
- Names or identities of individual consumers
- Contact information of consumers
- Individual viewing history of any consumer
- Personal data of any consumer

### 5.3 Service Providers
We may share your data with trusted third-party service providers:
- **Cloud Hosting**: AWS, Google Cloud for data storage
- **Analytics Tools**: Google Analytics, Firebase for app performance
- **Communication Services**: Email and notification providers
- **Payment Processors**: If paid features are introduced (e.g., Razorpay)
- **Verification Services**: FSSAI verification (if implemented)

All service providers are contractually bound to protect your data.

### 5.4 Legal Requirements
We may disclose your information if required by law:
- Court orders, subpoenas, or legal processes
- Government or regulatory authority requests
- FSSAI or health authority inquiries
- Prevention of fraud or illegal activity
- Protection of our rights and safety

### 5.5 Business Transfers
In the event of a merger, acquisition, or sale of assets, your information may be transferred to the acquiring entity. We will notify you of such changes.

### 5.6 With Your Consent
We may share your information for other purposes with your explicit consent.

### 5.7 What We NEVER Share
We will NEVER:
- Sell your personal information to third parties
- Share your email or phone with consumers
- Provide your personal contact details to advertisers
- Share consumer personal data with you (only aggregated analytics)

## 6. DATA RETENTION

We retain your data for different periods based on type and purpose:

- **Account Data**: Until you close your account, plus 90 days for operational/legal purposes
- **Mess Profile Information**: Until you remove your listing or close your account
- **Thali and Menu Data**: Until you delete items or close your account
- **Photos**: Until you remove them or close your account
- **Analytics Data**: Up to 24 months for historical reporting
- **Communication Records**: Up to 3 years for support and dispute resolution
- **Legal/Compliance Data**: Longer if required by law (e.g., FSSAI regulations)

When you close your account:
- Your public profile is removed from the consumer app
- Your account credentials and personal data are deleted after 90 days
- Aggregated, anonymized historical data may be retained for analytics

## 7. DATA SECURITY

We implement robust security measures to protect your business information:

**Technical Measures:**
- **Encryption**: Data in transit (HTTPS/TLS) and at rest (AES-256)
- **Authentication**: Secure login with password requirements
- **Access Controls**: Limited employee access on a need-to-know basis
- **Regular Backups**: Daily encrypted backups of your data
- **Vulnerability Testing**: Regular security audits and penetration testing

**Organizational Measures:**
- Employee confidentiality agreements
- Security training for staff
- Incident response procedures
- Data handling policies

**Your Responsibility:**
- Keep your login credentials secure
- Use strong, unique passwords
- Enable two-factor authentication (if available)
- Log out after using shared devices
- Report suspicious activity immediately

However, no security system is completely foolproof. We cannot guarantee absolute security.

## 8. YOUR RIGHTS UNDER INDIAN LAW

Under the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023, you have the following rights:

### 8.1 Right to Access
You can request access to all personal data we hold about you:
- Your account information
- Mess profile and listing data
- Analytics and engagement metrics
- Communication records

### 8.2 Right to Correction
You can update or correct inaccurate or incomplete information:
- Through the Business App's profile settings
- By contacting our support team
- By submitting a formal correction request

### 8.3 Right to Erasure (Right to be Forgotten)
You can request deletion of your data:
- Close your account through the app
- Request complete data deletion
- We will remove your mess listing from the consumer app

**Note**: We may retain certain data if required by law or for legitimate purposes (e.g., fraud prevention, dispute resolution).

### 8.4 Right to Data Portability
You can request a copy of your data in a structured format:
- Your mess profile information
- Thali and menu data
- Photos (links to download)
- Analytics reports (CSV or PDF)

### 8.5 Right to Withdraw Consent
You can withdraw consent at any time for:
- Marketing communications (opt-out via app settings)
- Non-essential data processing
- Future use of your information

**Note**: Withdrawing consent may limit your ability to use certain features.

### 8.6 Right to Nominate
You can nominate another individual to exercise your rights in the event of your death or incapacity.

**To exercise these rights**, contact us at www.khaneme.com or email our Grievance Officer.

## 9. FSSAI AND REGULATORY COMPLIANCE

### 9.1 FSSAI Information
- FSSAI number submission is optional but strongly recommended
- We do NOT verify FSSAI numbers with FSSAI authorities
- You are solely responsible for maintaining valid FSSAI licenses
- You must display your FSSAI license prominently at your mess premises

### 9.2 Your Responsibility
You are responsible for:
- Obtaining and maintaining valid FSSAI licenses
- Complying with all food safety regulations
- Ensuring hygiene and safety standards at your mess
- Accurate representation of your FSSAI status

### 9.3 Reporting
If we receive complaints about your FSSAI compliance or food safety:
- We may contact you for clarification
- We may temporarily suspend your listing pending investigation
- We may share information with FSSAI authorities if required by law
- Repeated violations may result in permanent removal from the platform

